          %ul
            %li
              %p
                Specifically the initial objects of
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Set"} Set
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cat"} Cat
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Top"} Top
                are all strict.
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/John+Baez"} John Baez
                showed on the
                %a{:href => "https://categorytheory.zulipchat.com/#narrow/stream/229199-learning.3A-questions/topic/Integers.20and.20rational.20numbers.20as.20strict.20initial.20objects.3F/near/422742440"} Category Theory Zulip
                that the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/rational+numbers"} rational numbers
                are a strict initial object in the category of
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/characteristic+zero"} characteristic zero
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fields"} fields
                and
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ring+homomorphisms"} ring homomorphisms
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ordered+fields"} ordered fields
                and
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ring+homomorphisms"} ring homomorphisms
            %li
              %p
                In the
                %a{:href => "https://categorytheory.zulipchat.com/#narrow/stream/229199-learning.3A-questions/topic/Integers.20and.20rational.20numbers.20as.20strict.20initial.20objects.3F/near/422749731"} same discussion thread on the Category Theory Zulip
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Madeleine+Birchfield"} Madeleine Birchfield
                showed that the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/integers"} integers
                are a strict initial object in the category of
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ordered+integral+domains"} ordered integral domains
                and
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monotonic+function"} strictly monotonic
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ring+homomorphisms"} ring homomorphisms
          %p
            At the other extreme, a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/zero+object"} zero object
            is a strict initial object only if the category is trivial (i.e.
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+of+categories"} equivalent
            to the
